* s1rcolor.scheme
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* dash translation of Stata's s1rcolor ("s1 reverse color") graph scheme.
*
* Source Stata scheme file : /Applications/StataNow/ado/base/s/scheme-s1rcolor.scheme
*                            (Stata #include chain: s2color -> s1color -> s1rcolor;
*                             byte-identical under /Applications/Stata/ado/base)
* Stata version            : StataNow 19.5 (MP), born 12 Aug 2026
* Extracted (UTC)          : 2026-09-18T18:58:04Z
* Translated (UTC)         : 2026-09-18
* Derived from             : test/fixtures/scheme_truth.json, key "s1rcolor",
*                            generated by scripts/extract_scheme_truth.py from
*                            Stata's own scheme-*.scheme and style/*.style files.
*
* Regenerate the fixture and re-check this file whenever Stata is upgraded:
* the values below were true of the Stata version named above and of no other.
*
* Colours are written as RESOLVED #rrggbb hex, not Stata colour names, on
* purpose.  SchemeParser._color() swallows a colour token OptionTranslator
* cannot resolve and substitutes its "#000000" default, so a name outside
* OptionTranslator._COLOR_MAP silently renders the series black.  Hex is
* self-contained and cannot fail that way.
*
* s1rcolor is the reverse-video scheme: the canvas, plot region and legend are
* genuinely black here, and the heading, axis lines and legend border are
* white.  The black backgrounds below are Stata's own resolved values, not the
* unresolvable-token fallback described above.
*
* This file is flat and standalone - no #include.  Stata's s1rcolor inherits
* most of its body from s1color (and s1color from s2color), but the fixture
* records the fully resolved post-include values, so every directive is
* spelled out here.
*
* Property categories dash's SchemeParser reads:
*   color, symbol, linepattern, linewidth, intensity, gsize, graphsize,
*   symbolsize, clockdir, numstyle
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

label "s1 reverse color"

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Background and region colors
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
color background      #000000
color plotregion      #000000
color legend          #000000
color legend_line     #ffffff
color major_grid      #505050
color minor_grid      #808080
color heading         #ffffff
color axisline        #ffffff

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Per-plot color cycle (p1-p15)
* s1rcolor resolves p#, p#line, p#bar and p#mark to the same colour: Stata
* sets only "color p1".."color p15" and every stub falls back to it (fixture
* sources: p_line_colors[i] <- "color p{i}", likewise bar and mark).  dash's
* parser has no stub fallback, so each family is written out in full.
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
color p1      #ffff00
color p2      #00ff00
color p3      #0080ff
color p4      #ff00ff
color p5      #ff7f00
color p6      #ff0000
color p7      #add8e6
color p8      #ffe474
color p9      #00ff80
color p10     #c0dcc0
color p11     #ff4500
color p12     #0000ff
color p13     #ff0080
color p14     #6e8e84
color p15     #a0522d

* Per-plot line color (for line/connected plots)
color p1line   #ffff00
color p2line   #00ff00
color p3line   #0080ff
color p4line   #ff00ff
color p5line   #ff7f00
color p6line   #ff0000
color p7line   #add8e6
color p8line   #ffe474
color p9line   #00ff80
color p10line  #c0dcc0
color p11line  #ff4500
color p12line  #0000ff
color p13line  #ff0080
color p14line  #6e8e84
color p15line  #a0522d

* Per-plot bar/area fill color
color p1bar    #ffff00
color p2bar    #00ff00
color p3bar    #0080ff
color p4bar    #ff00ff
color p5bar    #ff7f00
color p6bar    #ff0000
color p7bar    #add8e6
color p8bar    #ffe474
color p9bar    #00ff80
color p10bar   #c0dcc0
color p11bar   #ff4500
color p12bar   #0000ff
color p13bar   #ff0080
color p14bar   #6e8e84
color p15bar   #a0522d

* Per-plot marker fill color (scatter)
color p1mark   #ffff00
color p2mark   #00ff00
color p3mark   #0080ff
color p4mark   #ff00ff
color p5mark   #ff7f00
color p6mark   #ff0000
color p7mark   #add8e6
color p8mark   #ffe474
color p9mark   #00ff80
color p10mark  #c0dcc0
color p11mark  #ff4500
color p12mark  #0000ff
color p13mark  #ff0080
color p14mark  #6e8e84
color p15mark  #a0522d

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Marker symbol cycle
* Stata's s1rcolor declares no per-plot symbol at all: all 15 resolve through
* the bare "symbol p" class default, which is circle (fixture sources:
* p_symbols[i] <- "symbol p").  dash's parser reads "symbol p{i}" by exact
* key, so the constant cycle is written out.
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
symbol p1     circle
symbol p2     circle
symbol p3     circle
symbol p4     circle
symbol p5     circle
symbol p6     circle
symbol p7     circle
symbol p8     circle
symbol p9     circle
symbol p10    circle
symbol p11    circle
symbol p12    circle
symbol p13    circle
symbol p14    circle
symbol p15    circle

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Line patterns for line/connected plots
* As with symbols, all 15 resolve through the bare "linepattern p" default:
* s1rcolor distinguishes series by colour, never by dash pattern.
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
linepattern p1line   solid
linepattern p2line   solid
linepattern p3line   solid
linepattern p4line   solid
linepattern p5line   solid
linepattern p6line   solid
linepattern p7line   solid
linepattern p8line   solid
linepattern p9line   solid
linepattern p10line  solid
linepattern p11line  solid
linepattern p12line  solid
linepattern p13line  solid
linepattern p14line  solid
linepattern p15line  solid

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Line widths (Stata linewidth style names; "medium" is .30 Stata units)
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
linewidth p           medium
linewidth major_grid  medium

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Fill intensities
* "intensity area" is not set by any Stata base scheme; s1rcolor resolves it
* through the bare "intensity" class default, which is full (alpha 1.0).  It
* is recorded here under the key dash's parser actually reads.
* Note that "intensity bar" is inten80 in s1rcolor, not the full of s2color.
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
intensity p        inten80
intensity bar      inten80
intensity area     full

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Font sizes (Stata gsize keywords, relative units)
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
gsize text          medium
gsize heading       large
gsize axis_title    medsmall
gsize tick_label    medsmall
gsize note          small

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Graph dimensions, in inches (consumed by section 10 for figure proportions)
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
graphsize x  5.5
graphsize y  4

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Default marker size for the p cycle
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
symbolsize p  medium

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Legend placement
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
clockdir legend_position  6
numstyle legend_cols      2

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Major grid switches, as Stata's s1rcolor declares them.  SchemeParser
* stores these in _props but _init_properties() exposes no attribute for
* them yet; recorded so the declared value is available when a consumer
* lands, and so the value is not lost from the translation.
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
yesno draw_major_hgrid  no
yesno draw_major_grid   no
